            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion and continuous interest in 'mini.nvim'!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, Neovim doesn't provide any exported functionality to track/get/set dot-repeat action. I know that because there was a need for this in 'mini.operators', but the best way was [to use some hack](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2e2931b3822bf357d2f69cbc0bcb2d99a3f0d4c8/lua/mini/operators.lua#L1258-L1264).\r\n\r\nIn general, dot-repeat in both Neovim and Vim is implemented in the [part of C code base](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/d3fa8adea9ba4dcf96ec05aafff1a0cdb67a6d72/src/nvim/getchar.c#L444-L593) which was not touched pretty much since before Neovim was born. So I imagine it would require much effort to export any functionality related to this.\r\n\r\nClosing with \"I'd really love to support this, but it needs upstream changes which are quite unlikely to happen\".",
